--- body ---
## Context

`make check` on main in the primary checkout fails
`tests/test_resident_census.py::test_channel_budgets`: the skills channel is
7784 chars against a 7000 budget. The same commit passes in a fresh worktree
and in CI, so the gate is red only where an agent actually runs it.

Cause: the primary checkout carries UNTRACKED symlinks
`skills/{email,infrastructure,directory}` -> `~/.config/harness/private/skills/<name>`
(the private overlay, present since 2026-10-02). `scripts/resident_census.py`
counts `_name_and_description` for every `skills/*/SKILL.md` glob hit and
follows those links; a clean worktree does not have them. Measured at the raid
wave base commit fc0a75d8355817400b4370824f5314fa212d7c5a: 6952 chars without
the links, 7784 with them (+832). Reproduced by copying the three links into a
clean worktree at that commit — identical failure, identical count.

Same class as closed ticket 0989 (idh tests read the real checkout's untracked
private overlay links), which fixed the adapter/lifecycle fixtures through
`tests/tracked_tree.py`; the census was not covered by that fix.

Two facts must not be conflated. The private skill descriptions really are
resident in a session started in the primary checkout, so the token cost is
real. The budget in `tests/test_resident_census.py` is argued against the
tracked harness content, and that is what the overlay breaks.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `make check` passes both in the primary checkout and in a clean worktree on the same commit
- [x] The census states which skills it counted and whether private overlay links were present, so a real all-clear is distinguishable from a census that never saw the overlay (the docstring already treats a consumer project's own CLAUDE.md as extra)
- [x] The budget decision is argued here, not made silently: trim the private descriptions, raise the skills budget with the +832 stated, or measure the overlay as a separate channel the tracked-content gate does not fail on
- [x] Positive control: planting the three links in a worktree reproduces the failure the fix claims to handle, and their absence leaves the census green

## Raid plan — 2026-10-13

Budget decision: keep the 7000-character cap on tracked harness skill cards. Local private cards remain real resident cost and must be separately visible, with their inventory, presence/absence (or unknown classification), subtotal and contribution to the real session total. Neither raise the cap nor silently omit their cost.

Actions: classify cards from the Git index, including tracked directory symlinks and untracked ordinary directories, rather than symlink type alone. Preserve existing budgeted channel contracts and downstream total semantics; show unknown when tracking cannot be inspected. Metadata-free roots must still report their full observed cost conservatively.

First test: clean tracked tree plus the three local overlay links; preserve the clean tracked subtotal, display all links and +832 chars, include supplemental cost in the session total. Positive control demonstrates that counting the combined cards under the old cap reproduces the original overflow. Cover absence, tracked links and unavailable tracking.

Files: scripts/resident_census.py; tests/test_resident_census.py; this ticket. Reuse tests/tracked_tree.py and stdlib tools; no new copying layer or dependency. Exit criteria unchanged.


## Execution evidence — 2026-10-13

Kept the skills cap at 7000. The Git index classifies file cards and tracked
directory symlinks; untracked links and ordinary directories enter supplemental
`skills-local`. Both report modes enumerate every observed skill and state local
link presence or unknown tracking. Session totals include the supplement;
metadata-free roots retain all observed cost in the budgeted skills channel.

The old census from wave base `30a46f85995d8064762570abadf519deade1d1a9`
charges the planted cards as 7784 vs 6952 clean, reproducing the old overflow.
The real selected cards measure email275 + infrastructure275 + directory282 =832.
Code commit `0de58dd4` preserves 6952 tracked +832 local, and session totals
43162 clean /43994 with links. The contained checkout at that exact commit,
`/tmp/t1091-primary-overlay-check`, carries the three exact live symlink targets
and passed full `make check` (1606passed,4skipped). The actual primary checkout
was not modified or run at the new commit; its literal criterion remains for
post-merge verification. This contained same-code comparison is the authorized
pre-merge proxy, not a claim that the primary already runs the new census.

First census regression run:3failed,5passed. Fixed controls:8passed; check-fast:
964passed; declared adherence (`Makefile:31`, `make lint`):185passed. The first
clean full gate had1605passed,4skipped and one sandbox environment failure:
`test_index_injected_for_a_worktree_of_this_repository` requires write access
to Git worktree metadata. Rerun the full gate with that metadata access before PR.


## Completed criteria — actual primary verification, 2026-10-13

This evidence supersedes the earlier candidate's pending-primary statement;
the historical code-commit measurements and initial environment failure above
remain preserved.

1. At `7e1f77b1928ee49de97990940fd4b24b3df49cc7`, full `make check`
   passed both in the actual primary checkout with its three live private
   links (1606 passed, 4 skipped, 76.91 seconds) and in the clean owned
   worktree (1606 passed, 4 skipped, 104.06 seconds). The primary was checked
   for cleanliness and foreign processes, temporarily detached at that SHA,
   then restored to `housekeeping-20261012` at
   `1e8ccb3874f2f7bd0c12be05ae3d35f1cc656b53` and verified clean.
   Evidence: `/tmp/t1091-actual-primary-manifest.log`,
   `/tmp/t1091-actual-primary-full.log`, and
   `/tmp/t1091-full-clean-final.log`.
2. Both report modes enumerate the counted skill paths and state local-link
   presence or unknown tracking. The actual primary's observed inventory
   reports 6952 tracked + 832 local chars and 43994 session chars, matching
   the contained overlay control; clean session cost is 43162 chars.
   Evidence: `/tmp/t1091-primary-observed-using-new-census.log` and the
   eight passing `tests/test_resident_census.py` controls.
3. The argued decision remains the Raid plan's 7000-char tracked cap, with
   supplemental local cost included in every session total. No cap changed.
4. The old census at wave base
   `30a46f85995d8064762570abadf519deade1d1a9` counts the planted cards as
   7784 chars versus 6952 without them, reproducing the old 7000-cap failure.
   Fixed same-commit clean, contained-overlay, and actual-primary full gates
   pass while retaining the measured 832-char cost.
   Evidence: `/tmp/t1091-old-overlay-control.log` and
   `/tmp/t1091-full-overlay-final.log`.

The final completion update changes this ticket only; census code and tests
remain identical to the same-commit actual-primary and clean-worktree gates.
